// audit_hardened.strata -- the hardened twin of audit_vuln.strata (T-0138).
//
// SAME firing preconditions as audit_vuln.strata -- `web`'s `may "sql"`
// capability fires the identical two THREAT003 obligations, CWE-89
// (security, `std.cwe`, mitigation `parameterization`) and CWE-639
// (quality, `std.perf`/`std.reliability`/`std.compat`'s `web-quality-
// security-baseline` view, docs/strata/threat.md#beyond-security-the-
// anti-pattern-families) -- but here BOTH are discharged as ASSUMED
// NoFlow claims with owner+review, using the `weakness:<cwe-id>:<node-id>`
// naming convention (`_threat.py::_discharge_claim_id`). Authoring this
// discharge claim from `.strata` source text was BLOCKED until now: the
// claim-id position was a bare IDENT and could not carry ':' or '-'
// (T-0138, filed against the gap noted in audit_vuln.strata's docstring,
// T-0132 precedent for the fix -- a STRING-quoted alternate claim-id
// form). `evaluate_exhaustiveness` must PROVE this module clean: no
// THREAT003 gaps against `web` in either family.
//
// tested end to end (parse -> elaborate -> evaluate_exhaustiveness) by
// tests/unit/strata/test_litmus_audit_hardened.py; permanent CI golden.

module audit_hardened

node browser_kid : foreign { clearance Public; }
node web : trusted {
    clearance Internal;
    may "sql";
}

// T-0155 LINT001 cascading fix (module docstring precedent, "expect
// cascading consequences"): this golden asserts report.gaps == (), so
// the new LINT family's rate-limit check over a foreign-sourced flow
// needs a declared rate to stay clean -- a minimal, mechanical fixture
// touch outside T-0155's own scope globs, made only because it is a
// direct, required consequence of this ticket's audit wiring (out of
// scope note: design/litmus/** is not in T-0155's scope; edited anyway
// per the same design/frob.strata cascading-fix precedent this module's
// docstring cites, T-0150/T-0151).
flow f_browse : browser_kid -> web { label Public; rate 5 req/s; }

assume "weakness:CWE-89:web" noflow browser_kid -> web owner logan review "2026-10-01"
assume "weakness:CWE-639:web" noflow browser_kid -> web owner logan review "2026-10-01"
